.\"	$NetBSD$
.\"
.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt RPC.TLSSERVD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rpc.tlsservd
.Nd TLS handshake daemon for RPC-with-TLS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dm
.Op Fl A Ar cafile
.Fl c Ar cert
.Fl k Ar key
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
performs the server side of the TLS 1.3 handshake of RPC-with-TLS
(RFC 9289) for the in-kernel ONC RPC server.
The kernel answers the
.Dv AUTH_TLS
probe itself and offers
.Dq STARTTLS
only while
.Nm
is running.
Each connection is taken with
.Xr nfssvc 2
.Dv NFSSVC_TLSWAIT
and handed back with
.Dv NFSSVC_TLSDONE ,
carrying the traffic secrets for the kernel's record layer and the
.Dq tls-exporter
channel binding (RFC 9266).
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl A Ar cafile
Verify client certificates against the certificates in
.Ar cafile .
.It Fl c Ar cert
The server's certificate chain, PEM.
.It Fl d
Stay in the foreground and log to standard error as well.
.It Fl k Ar key
The server's private key, PEM.
.It Fl m
Require a verified client certificate: mutual host authentication.
Without it clients may be anonymous, as RFC 9289 s4.2 allows.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nfssvc 2 ,
.Xr nfsd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 9289, RFC 9266, RFC 8446.
